# An unterminated string ending in `\`: just adding a quote would leave it open, so the help doubles the backslash.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where p == 'abc\
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..21
  PIPELINE@0..20
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..20
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..20
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "p"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        EQ2@12..14 "=="
        WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
        LITERAL@15..20
          STRING@15..20 "'abc\\"
  WHITESPACE@20..21 "\n"

error[DS0002]: unterminated string
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | t | where p == 'abc\
  |                ^^^^^ this string is never closed
  |
  = help: the `\` at the end escapes a quote; to end the string with a backslash, double it and add a closing `'`
  = note: a string ends at the end of its line
